IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pc70-nouns`
IMPORT `pc70-cross-references`

-- Row il-70. TESTS OF THE CONTROLS: the sound references kept beside the cited ones. They pass.
-- I1: the two sections the 1995 replacement adds to the list (239A, 239B) exist, because item 22 of the same instrument adds them; every other number of the list is typed as not read.
-- I2: the numbers other than 144A are typed as not read; the section the 2014 instruction edits is the section the 1986 instrument added.
-- The expected values are hand-written from the quotation lines in pc70-cross-references.l4 and from the printed pages, not copied from the values there.

§ `Tests of the controls`

-- I1 control: 239A and 239B are added by item 22 of SH 1533 (19.7.1995), the instrument that carries the replacement.
#ASSERT `the provision is added by an instrument deposited here` `Customs Ordinance section 239A`
#ASSERT `the provision is added by an instrument deposited here` `Customs Ordinance section 239B`
#ASSERT `the provision is not repealed by an instrument deposited here` `Customs Ordinance section 239A`
#ASSERT `the provision is not repealed by an instrument deposited here` `Customs Ordinance section 239B`
#ASSERT `Customs Ordinance section 239A`'s `the issue date printed on the instrument that gives the status` EQUALS JUST (Date 19 7 1995)
#ASSERT `Customs Ordinance section 239B`'s `the issue date printed on the instrument that gives the status` EQUALS JUST (Date 19 7 1995)
#ASSERT `Customs Ordinance section 239A`'s `the issue date printed on the instrument that gives the status` EQUALS JUST (`the 1995 instruction on section 29C`'s `the issue date its footer prints`)

-- I1 control: the list as the 1995 instruction leaves it names 239A and 239B, and the provisions the row did not read are the other seventeen, each typed NotChecked.
#ASSERT elem "239A" (`item I1: section 29C cites sections 128, 170 and 171 of the Customs Ordinance`'s `the tokens of the list after the instructions read`)
#ASSERT elem "239B" (`item I1: section 29C cites sections 128, 170 and 171 of the Customs Ordinance`'s `the tokens of the list after the instructions read`)
#ASSERT count (`item I1: section 29C cites sections 128, 170 and 171 of the Customs Ordinance`'s `the provisions the row did not read`) EQUALS 17
#ASSERT all `the provision was not read` (`item I1: section 29C cites sections 128, 170 and 171 of the Customs Ordinance`'s `the provisions the row did not read`)
#ASSERT NOT (elem "128" (map `the number of the provision` (`item I1: section 29C cites sections 128, 170 and 171 of the Customs Ordinance`'s `the provisions the row did not read`)))
#ASSERT NOT (elem "170" (map `the number of the provision` (`item I1: section 29C cites sections 128, 170 and 171 of the Customs Ordinance`'s `the provisions the row did not read`)))
#ASSERT NOT (elem "171" (map `the number of the provision` (`item I1: section 29C cites sections 128, 170 and 171 of the Customs Ordinance`'s `the provisions the row did not read`)))
#ASSERT NOT (elem "239A" (map `the number of the provision` (`item I1: section 29C cites sections 128, 170 and 171 of the Customs Ordinance`'s `the provisions the row did not read`)))
#ASSERT NOT (elem "239B" (map `the number of the provision` (`item I1: section 29C cites sections 128, 170 and 171 of the Customs Ordinance`'s `the provisions the row did not read`)))
#ASSERT elem "231C" (map `the number of the provision` (`item I1: section 29C cites sections 128, 170 and 171 of the Customs Ordinance`'s `the provisions the row did not read`))
#ASSERT count (`item I1: section 29C cites sections 128, 170 and 171 of the Customs Ordinance`'s `the provisions the row checked`) EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `the provision was not read` `Customs Ordinance section 128` EQUALS FALSE

-- I2 control: the numbers other than 144A are not read by this row (four of them, each typed NotChecked), and 144A is not among them.
#ASSERT count (`item I2: section 29D cites section 144A of the Value Added Tax Law`'s `the provisions the row did not read`) EQUALS 4
#ASSERT all `the provision was not read` (`item I2: section 29D cites section 144A of the Value Added Tax Law`'s `the provisions the row did not read`)
#ASSERT NOT (elem "144A" (map `the number of the provision` (`item I2: section 29D cites section 144A of the Value Added Tax Law`'s `the provisions the row did not read`)))
#ASSERT elem "102A" (map `the number of the provision` (`item I2: section 29D cites section 144A of the Value Added Tax Law`'s `the provisions the row did not read`))
#ASSERT map `the number of the provision` (`item I2: section 29D cites section 144A of the Value Added Tax Law`'s `the provisions the row did not read`) EQUALS LIST "1A", "102A", "106", "112A"
#ASSERT count (`item I2: section 29D cites section 144A of the Value Added Tax Law`'s `the provisions the row checked`) EQUALS 1

-- Controls for both items: the sections the later instructions edit are the sections SH 1195 item 44(3) added.
#ASSERT `the 2014 instruction on section 29D`'s `the section of the Law it names` EQUALS `Purchase Tax Law section 29D`'s `its number, with letters in Latin`
#ASSERT `the 1995 instruction on section 29C`'s `the section of the Law it names` EQUALS `Purchase Tax Law section 29C`'s `its number, with letters in Latin`
#ASSERT `the provision is added by an instrument deposited here` `Purchase Tax Law section 29D`
#ASSERT `the provision is added by an instrument deposited here` `Purchase Tax Law section 29C`
#ASSERT `Purchase Tax Law section 29D`'s `the issue date printed on the instrument that gives the status` EQUALS JUST (Date 24 8 1986)
